      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before this there\u0027s a state on disk where we have an SDM file without its corresponding SDC file. Please add some comments to runtime/oat/sdc_file.h to lay down what applies to that state, something like this:\n\n- The SDC file augments the OAT files in the corresponding SDM file, so without it the SDM file is incomplete. That means:\n  - The runtime ignores an SDM file without a corresponding SDC.\n  - ART Service generates the corresponding SDC on dexopt if it is missing or stale.\n  - Other processes like the file GC considers an SDM file without a corresponding SDC invalid and may clean it up. This may race with a package installation before the SDC is created, but it\u0027s rare and the effect is recoverable, so it\u0027s considered acceptable.",
